  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [`putImageData`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#dom-context-2d-putimagedata) function reads:\n\n> The putImageData() method writes data from ImageData structures back to the rendering context's output bitmap.\n\nThe implication here is that there is a straight `memcpy` occurring, and that this operation could be performed by a DMA engine (as opposed to a more general purpose blitter). This has never been the case. `ImageData` is unpremultiplied and 2D canvas is premultiplied, so, at a minimum, alpha-multiplication is occurring in this operation. This API is also expected to do color conversion, although that was added later.\n\nIn practice, `putImageData(imageData, dstX, dstY, srcX, srcY, w, h)` is equivalent to:\n```\n  ctx.save();\n  ctx.resetTransform();\n  ctx.globalCompositeOperation = \"copy\"; // note that this does the alpha multiply\n  // maybe state needs to get set?\n  ctx.drawImage(imageData, srcX, srcY, w, h, dstX, dstY, w, h);\n  ctx.restore();\n```\n\nThe above doesn't actually work, because `ImageData` is not a `CanvasImageSource`. It may be that we should expand this issue to update that as well.",
